@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+These are source-only dispatch fragments for the reserved memory-original
+PostgreSQL156 / SQLite75 migration. Merge them into the complete corresponding
+memory-original UP/DOWN source after the inventory155 / inventory74 migration
+exists and after the atomic execution/derivation/checkpoint schema is merged.
+They are deliberately outside the runtime migration directories. They must not
+be applied alone or exposed through runtime AutoMigrate/backfill.
+
+Every real original admission creates its exact dispatch intent in the same
+transaction as pending/revision binding. A broker response is only retry
+metadata. Completion requires VerifyMemoryOriginalCompletion to prove the
+append-only execution, derivation, operations and full drained checkpoint.
+Absent that atomic producer/verifier, the relay retains and refuses dispatch;
+the first-slice base by itself is not an accepted implementation.
+
+No dispatch payload is reconstructed from current messages, config or current
+queue state. No legacy pending row receives a dispatch. No observed dispatch
+may be deleted, even after completion. DOWN must refuse while facts exist.
+
+Failed original validation produces a typed retry claim containing only an
+immutable-row fingerprint and static failure code. It has no executable payload
+grant. The row receives retry/lease metadata and retains original bytes and
+pending work so a corrupt earliest intent cannot permanently monopolize the
+normal relay scan. Completion/enqueue must refuse a failed validation claim.
+
+Lite consumers are owned by SyncTaskExecutor: Stop rejects new enqueue, cancels
+scheduled/retry waits and active task contexts, and waits for handler return.
+The executor cleanup is registered before relay startup; ResourceCleaner LIFO
+therefore joins the relay first and the executor second. A handler that ignores
+cancellation still prevents a successful join until it actually returns. SQL DB
+close is not registered by this source, so no actual DB-close ordering gate is
+claimed. Cancellation never creates a successful original completion receipt.
