+This is a source-only policy producer slice on frozen 5e071eef. PostgreSQL156
+and SQLite75 are already reserved by memory_original_admissions; the policy
+fragments are appended to those pending UP files and prepended to their DOWN
+files. They are not additional guessed migration versions or live migrations.
+Full PostgreSQL153→154→155→156 / SQLite72→73→74→75 acceptance remains required.
+The component SQL fixtures install the existing reserved pending schema; they
+do not certify the missing inventory155/74 full chain.
+
+The settings full replacement calls ReplaceMemoryPolicyOriginal. Its real
+current actor/effective role and configured DirectoryRuntime are resolved on
+the same transaction connection; runtime routing locks precede permission
+epochs, and the final role check happens while current actor controls are held.
+No client origin ID or cached owner role authorizes the write. Generic tenant
+CRUD remains an unproved writer, not a policy authoring boundary.
+
+An authorized replacement commits exact normalized policy bytes, a retained
+current revision, an append-only original, body152 capture, and an append-only
+body receipt together. The receipt fixes the original slot/body/head revision
+and source identity. The policy body is an inline mirror, not a policy-body
+cache created by a worker. Body capture absence, schema absence, missing heads,
+missing journal, changed receipt or unavailable original body refuses.
+The producer's private boundary records the actual complete empty-KB lease
+scope for the independent new settings input; inventory cannot backfill it.
+
+Migration initialization records UNKNOWN controls only. Raw SQL/CRUD changes,
+soft/hard deletion, recreation and ABA advance retained revisions without
+creating an origin. Only absence of a current-version origin is classified
+UNKNOWN. An observed origin with missing/unsafe body evidence refuses full
+authoring; it is not silently reclassified as a legacy root.
+
+A new complete human replacement may author a new root after a raw gap. It
+cannot become a descendant of a policy queued before that gap. When the old
+current original is valid, the writer alone records its successor edge. Queue
+capture pins original origin/revision/digests/body receipt without rewriting
+the message input admission. Execution may choose a genuinely authored current
+descendant, then pins that exact policy fact for the whole model result. Even
+same-byte reauthoring after the model starts refuses the old execution.
+
+Scheduling capture and execution acquire real body152 read leases over every
+policy origin used in the chain. The per-read context fixes owner/body/epoch
+and exact heads; final same-TX checks include journal, physical availability
+and a fresh SQL-clock TTL check after the last physical read. A fixed15-minute
+policy lease covers the existing9-minute model window; no deadline is widened.
+Close releases only those actual leases outside the business transaction;
+cleanup errors cannot produce a successful caller return. There is no policy
+heartbeat or instant policy-change model cancellation claim: changes are
+refused before the call or before atomic result commit.
+
+SOURCE ONLY: formatting, compilation and all real SQL/application tests have
+not been run. The new tests declare six SQLite/PostgreSQL parents and52 leaves,
+including eight genuine custom-policy/successor positives. The old515 material
+fixture and its business expectations remain byte-identical; the existing
+atomic fixture setup uses the genuine policy writer, preserving its assertions.
+Do not interpret these drafts as acceptance of the older unwired515 fixture.
+
+The complete model-original producer is still missing. Model/current-selector
+hash checks in the base are not upgraded into genuine model origins here.
+Productive partial resume/derived-memory inputs, policy lifecycle closure,
+full155/74 migrations, whole memory regression gates, and normal application
+acceptance remain pending. No overall memory or body-retention gate is closed.
