+SOURCE ONLY model producer component, based on sealed policy ac883341.
+No formatting, compilation, Go, SQL, Docker or application execution was done.
+The six declared SQLite/PostgreSQL parents contain52 planned leaves, including
+the genuine Create→Schedule→outbox Relay→Handle result/receipt path and early/
+late definition, credential and state withdrawal. They are not PASS evidence.
+
+These are fragments of already-reserved PostgreSQL156 / SQLite75. The UP is
+appended after memory/policy, and DOWN precedes it. Existing models receive
+UNKNOWN retained controls only; no original is backfilled. Full inventory155/
+74 and the complete prior chain remain separate acceptance requirements.
+
+Human model creation/replacement writes exact definition, persisted credential
+ciphertext, state, body152 capture and immutable exact-body receipts in one TX.
+Definition excludes APIKey/AppSecret and operational Status/IsDefault/ManagedBy.
+Credential originals bind actual persisted ciphertext and its strict decoded
+plaintext fingerprint; a new Value() encryption nonce is never worker proof.
+CustomHeaders/ExtraConfig/AppID/Spec and every other consumed parameter remain
+fully covered by the definition body/receipt and its lease.
+
+Partial model editing requires the real old original proof supplied by the
+internal GetModelByID boundary, plus its same-current proof at write time.
+The HTTP caller cannot provide that gorm/json-hidden proof. This prevents a
+stale handler's inherited secrets from being relabeled as new human bytes.
+Credential operations mutate only the actual locked old object with valid
+definition/credential parents. No-op clear retains its original epoch.
+UNKNOWN legacy may be explicitly FULL reauthored with a new literal input;
+partial edits and unsafe observed facts refuse. Full reauthoring is an internal
+API here; no new public full-replacement handler was added.
+
+Status completion consumes the original creation proof and republishes only
+state. A download may not rewrite a definition or adopt changed credentials.
+The asynchronous service copies the original name/proof and rechecks the real
+current author; it does not publish the old mutable whole Model. SQL raw writes,
+ABA, soft/hard removal and recreation retain monotonic controls without facts.
+Defaults/ManagedBy changes are separate state controls; raw writers invalidate
+them and do not become original authoring. State evidence is metadata authority,
+not a proof of downloaded weights or an actual successful remote model call.
+
+Queue and execution pin the actual definition/credential/state proof and both
+original-body receipts. Model reads acquire actual owner/body/epoch leases;
+every final check fixes heads, journal and fresh SQL-clock TTL after physical
+IO. Existing worker9-minute bounds are unchanged; body leases are15 minutes.
+Model instance construction in GetChatModel consumes the held snapshot only,
+with explicit provider/base URL/credential, never current tenant credentials
+or default Ollama environment. The bounded transport fixture first constructs
+that real production instance before replacing its roundtrip, so configuration
+capability cannot be faked by a metadata-only model spy.
+
+The instance/source slice supports explicitly configured remote Chat models.
+Configured nonzero-tenant builtins require a real active DB system administrator
+to author; a cached context flag is insufficient. Cross-tenant ordinary models
+are refused, while genuinely authored builtin visibility is retained.
+
+REMAINING, not replaced by raw invalidation: builtin Tenant0 platform namespace;
+trusted YAML/file authoring and default writers; original configured Ollama
+runtime endpoint/download proof; credential fallbacks to tenant/platform config;
+embedding/rerank/VLM/ASR construction and other ordinary consumers that lack a
+model lifetime context. GetChatModel fails closed
+without a model lifetime context; ordinary callers must be wired before this
+source can be promoted. No model module/full memory/application gate is closed.
+
+Historical metadata-only material is implemented separately. It loads the exact
+execution definition/opaque credential/state facts and original body receipts,
+without ModelParameters.Scan/decryption, returning no Model/secret. Actual
+current actor/read permissions and tenant/model visibility remain mandatory.
+Known authorized definition/credential successors keep A's original material
+readable; raw/UNKNOWN/recreated-root gaps refuse. Current soft/hard deletion and
+its retained state epoch are retirement controls and close historical reads.
+Downloading/download_failed are operational availability states, not retirement;
+their genuine state publication alone does not invalidate completed history.
+The original execution still requires its own active state fact. Neither this
+reader nor its context authorizes construction/calling the old model.
+
+Historical holds have a separate proof-digest map, leaving B's exact CURRENT
+model hold intact. Same-TX CheckHistoricalModelOriginalHolds rechecks physical
+body, original head/receipt, journal, live owner/epoch/TTL and current controls.
+The production bridge parses immutable Execution.ModelProofJSON and verifies
+execution digest; it depends on the separately prepared derived authority
+interface and must be fused with that source before compilation. Missing factory
+capability remains closed. Two additional parents/16 provider leaves are drafts;
+the derived agent owns the complete genuine A→B business/receipt regression.
+
+Fixture setup carries the exact a35 empty Organization/OrganizationTenantMember/
+PermissionVersion schema correction. Existing resource-tuple/shared-agent fixes
+from Root's newer native/policy integration still require three-way fusion.
+Old515 business assertions are unchanged; only its shared transport helper gains
+real model construction/lifetime capability. The sealed ac883 rollback fixture
+context identity bug is fixed only in this child slice using an inherited
+test-owned marker, preserving real cancel and rollback assertions.
